id: pm-rust-xb3s
title: Implement native context history and dependency orientation with oracle parity
description: "Brief context, verified history reads, dependency listing, large public tracker latency and exact gates against the pinned oracle."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: conformance,orientation,rust
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:01:55.242Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T13:38:16.996Z"
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[41]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T03:02:15.486Z",codex-agent,"Plan: implement native brief context focus selection and packing, append-only history reads, and dependency tree reads. Compare complete CLI bytes against the locked oracle on disposable trackers. Document unsupported flags explicitly, retain release disablement, and record revert controls, large public tracker latency and all local/platform gates. Pinned history reads do not verify by default; --verify returns a verification report rather than refusing on a broken record hash. Preserve this observable oracle behavior and document the distinction."
  "2026-10-18T03:15:21.835Z",codex-agent,"Implementation in progress: native brief relevance ordering and identity packing, compact/full history with strict integrity exit, and bounded dependency tree/graph reads. Initial local build succeeds. Added real-CLI fixed-clock differential fixtures; extending refusal and corruption cases before the aggregate gate. CLI orientation requires a complete initialized settings document; fixtures now use real pm init rather than a partial settings surrogate."
  "2026-10-18T03:39:06.493Z",codex-agent,"First real-CLI differential: history passed, including immutable-author tampering with --verify --strict-exit. Dependency truncation exposed an internal row-contract token estimate, now matched. Context exposed an oracle behavior: the 25 ms packing deadline can expire before the first selection when this shared host deschedules Node, returning zero focus rows and suggestions despite active candidates. The orientation fixture now pins the monotonic clock as well as Date to test deterministic bytes. Native packing completes deterministically; document this timing boundary and report it as an oracle UX gap rather than claiming scheduling equivalence."
  "2026-10-18T04:12:46.206Z",codex-agent,"The six-test orientation differential passed: context focus/budgets/cursors, history integrity and retained rewrite evidence, dependency traversal/refusals, explicit unsupported options, read-only storage during concurrent unrelated writes, and group caps/session affinity. Added further weekly-calendar and bounded-history cases. Benchmark preflight found one closed weekly UTC event in the unchanged public-tracker copy; expanding that existing calendar shape instead of filtering the dataset. Local isolated strict health passed eight checks with four advisories; ambient health separately reports the global extension host-version skew. Timings and full coverage are still pending."
  "2026-10-18T04:28:26.178Z",codex-agent,"The extended native orientation differential suite passed 8 tests, including bounded large history, immutable record tampering, retained rewrite evidence, weekly recurrence, semantic and delivered usage affinity, and concurrent unrelated writes. The context reader now captures one authoritative corpus for ranking and summaries; its real-filesystem scan-count regression passed. Clippy all-targets deny-warnings passed. Draft PR #92 is open. Coverage, revert controls and the final shared-host timing receipt remain pending."
  "2026-10-18T04:34:38.482Z",codex-agent,"All three operating-system test jobs passed on the initial PR head. The Linux aggregate gate then correctly refused coverage below 100 percent: lines 99.3069, functions 99.3892, regions 99.2402, branches 96.5957. Boundary acceptance exposed and corrected a timestamp-unit mismatch in feedback retention, touch windows and deadline scoring; 26 orientation unit tests now pass. Additional budget, dispatch and integrity tests are being added without reducing gate thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T04:36:57.364Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: cargo test --locked --lib record_envelopes_and_replay_hashes failed 0 passed/1 failed when only record_error was replaced by its pre-slice no-verification behavior (None versus record_hash_mismatch). cargo test --locked --lib session_and_usage_affinity failed 0/1 when only affinity returned empty evidence (0 versus 3 claims). cargo test --locked --lib dependency_value_refusals failed 0/1 when only index discarded the new relationship rows (2 versus 3 nodes). Each control rebuilt successfully, failed an assertion, then restored its source bytes and verified SHA-256 equality. No counterfactual source is committed."
  "2026-10-18T04:52:19.946Z",codex-agent,"The mandatory pm test --run --progress completed successfully: 1 linked command, 9 differential tests passed, 0 failed. The positive library pass completed 218 tests and the orientation dispatch pass completed 2 tests. The subsequent array-test replay fix passed its targeted unit regression; its sealed real-oracle fixture and pre-command global refusal tests are included for the next full run. Private rustdoc and all-target Clippy passed before those two final dispatch/replay refinements; the current checks are running."
  "2026-10-18T05:11:09.371Z",codex-agent,"Current boundary work: 227 library tests passed after correcting a synthetic budget envelope to carry the summary a real context producer supplies. The prior candidate CI failures are retained as failed evidence. Real storage failures, incomplete RFC 6902 operands, multiple retained proof generations, legacy optional rows and a split-surrogate TOON refusal now have acceptance fixtures. Minimal static extension discovery has a real CLI differential fixture; richer manifest/policy diagnostics refuse explicitly and declared context_relevance overrides refuse even with health omitted. Benchmark runtimes use the same isolated global-user environment with the complete copied public tracker. Final aggregate gates and latency samples are pending."
  "2026-10-18T05:25:31.886Z",codex-agent,"Candidate e36b9bb CI and the first isolated local aggregate stopped at the unchanged Clippy 100-line function limit after expanding one test to 114 lines. The test is now split into API and cache/extension cases; all-target deny-warnings Clippy passed, and the restarted isolated aggregate passed fmt, Clippy and private rustdoc before entering all-target tests. Minimal-extension byte parity passed 1 real differential test; declared service refusal passed its targeted unit test. The 30-run benchmark has begun with a separate verified copy of the same locked 2026.10.14 oracle, isolated global user state, and a fixed release-binary fingerprint."
  "2026-10-18T05:52:53.655Z",codex-agent,"Additional behavioral proof: cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential history_reserved_patch_paths_match_oracle failed 0 passed/1 failed against the preceding verifier. A sealed two-record fixture made the oracle report verify_failed:patch_apply_failed:entry_2 while native reported a different replay-hash error for constructor/prototype. Adding the pinned codec prototype guard to destinations and copy/move sources made the identical test pass 1/0. Numeric exponent/hex control parity also passed 1/0. After cleaning only package build artifacts, the current library pass is 230/0 and all-target deny-warnings Clippy passed. The partial old-binary timing series and interrupted aggregate are not final evidence; both are being restarted for the corrected build."
  "2026-10-18T06:02:16.118Z",codex-agent,"The full 2991-item public tracker copy passed an additional exact context comparison with fixed wall/packing clocks and an isolated synthetic author: JSON stdout 11839 bytes and default TOON stdout 7219 bytes were identical, stderr empty, exits 0. Candidate b573b8b passed all three OS test jobs; its aggregate coverage exposed one unreachable context budget branch after the shared writer had already returned the same budget error. That redundant branch is removed. The corrected prototype verifier passed its sealed-record differential proof, 230 library tests passed, and current all-target Clippy passed. The release timing series and complete isolated aggregate will now run against this frozen production implementation."
  "2026-10-18T06:20:31.901Z",codex-agent,"The extension directory guard has a behavioral revert proof: removing only the new file-type guard makes context_cache_and_extension_boundaries fail on a symlink to a manifest declaring a context relevance override (exit 101); restoring the exact source bytes passes (1 test). A new real-process test covers strict verification success and a closed history output pipe, including unchanged history bytes. All three OS Rust test jobs pass at fa30341; aggregate coverage remains incomplete, so final gates and timing are being rerun against frozen source."
  "2026-10-18T06:27:43.840Z",codex-agent,"The final 30-run cold-process receipt is complete on the full 2991-item public tracker copy. Native/oracle p50 milliseconds: context 1067.7/1175.2, list 731.6/445.3, search history 787.4/1345.1, get 692.6/433.7. Native list/get are slower; record all results and track optimization separately. Effective nice 19; 4 CPUs, shared host; 1-minute load ranged 9.04 to 17.59. SHA-256 verification found zero changed files among all 6004 authoritative source files and their copied equivalents. Release binary source 22f7fd0; subsequent changes are acceptance fixtures only. Additional fixtures cover inherited tags, populated extension health, isolated usage-disable behavior and both retained-proof hash algorithms."
  "2026-10-18T06:31:02.841Z",codex-agent,"Windows Rust CI at 22f7fd0 exposed a real existing publisher defect: orientation concurrency failed 11 passed/1 failed because an unrelated item vanished between delete and rename. The replacement publisher now uses the standard replacement rename without a prior unlink, preserving existing locks and recovery journals. A deterministic real-filesystem test requires failed publication to preserve destination bytes. Reinstating the previous Windows delete-before-rename behavior portably on Linux made that test fail 0 passed/1 failed (exit 101); restoring exact source bytes passed 1/0. This is a behavioral control of the Windows sequence, not a Windows-local execution claim. The pre-fix pm-linked differential run passed 12/0; repeat on the final source. The previous incomplete aggregate is superseded. No coverage thresholds or exclusions changed."
  "2026-10-18T06:36:33.510Z",codex-agent,"The rename-only publisher passes its new destination-preservation test on Windows. The Windows run reached 233 passed/1 failed because an existing recovery assertion expected the removed DeleteFile operation error 32; replacement rename correctly returns access denied (5) for the held read-shared handle. Updated that Windows-only assertion to require both PermissionDenied and exact error 5, retaining all original unchanged-item/history, retained-journal, private-temporary cleanup and idempotent recovery assertions. Production code is unchanged after fe76d4b; the current release timing and Linux aggregate remain valid for that source."
  "2026-10-18T06:44:20.968Z",codex-agent,"Final production-source linked acceptance: pm test pm-rust-xb3s --run --progress executed cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential successfully, 12 passed/0 failed, exit 0, elapsed 392486 ms. This includes the concurrent readers/writer fixture. The CLI reports evidence_recording.recorded=false, reason=tracking_disabled; this comment is the persistent result receipt, and the project tracking policy is unchanged. Linux aggregate library and binary passes are 233/0 and 22/0; broader integration and branch coverage are still running. Clock-pinned final release context remains byte-identical on the complete public tracker copy (11839 JSON bytes and 7219 TOON bytes). The refreshed timing series runs with nice -n 0 at inherited effective priority 15; no shared-host priorities or services are changed."
  "2026-10-18T07:03:31.679Z",codex-agent,"The remaining aggregate coverage failure on 6cd9aa9 is identical on Linux/macOS: lines 11653/11653, functions 1170/1170, regions 19100/19101, branches 2825/2828. Added real API fixtures for a fitting nonempty context page, absent extension health and explicit rich-manifest refusal; added one owned argument-stream type covering hidden controls, close aliases and files/docs/test namespaces. Focused nightly acceptance passes 233 library and 23 binary tests; context branches are now 254/254, history 226/226 and deps 104/104. Argument-normalizer groups have zero missed regions. Remaining focused context functions are existing multi-blocked sorting closures exercised by the integration suite. All-target deny-warnings Clippy passes. No production code, thresholds or coverage exclusions changed. Restart the complete isolated aggregate with RUST_TEST_THREADS=8 to verify the frozen test source."
  "2026-10-18T07:16:18.384Z",codex-agent,"Completed refreshed release latency: 30 runs per command/runtime, 240 raw samples, effective nice 15. Native/oracle p50 ms: context 7407.5/10985.6, list 4807.6/4000.8, search history 6153.1/10507.0, get 4405.4/3715.0. Sampled one-minute load 20.07-44.97, with concurrent validation active; all values and p95s are in docs/NATIVE_ORIENTATION.md and its linked CSV/JSON. SHA-256 recheck again found zero changes across all 6004 original authoritative files and copied equivalents. The production rebuild preserves measured binary SHA-256 e0328e4750cc0347d09f3dd2d89255a4e02c0b4d2a79cf7a0d059a078dc10876. Additional real CLI acceptance covers an unknown flag on a non-orientation command: both ordinary and nightly runs pass 11/0; branch instrumentation confirms the optional orientation classifier takes its previously missing false path. Current all-target Clippy passes. No production source changes after fe76d4b."
  "2026-10-18T07:53:11.896Z",codex-agent,"Candidate 6687ef9 passed all functional suites (Linux 449, macOS 445, Windows 441) and Linux/macOS aggregate coverage at 100% in all four required dimensions. Windows completed all tests but its aggregate retained 3 missed regions, 2 lines and 2 branches solely at the standard Clap immediate-exit fallback in main. The non-orientation refusal case already passes, but immediate exit bypasses normal teardown there. Parser failures now print through Clap and return the same 0/2 status from main; no coverage-only condition is added. Six pre-change versus post-change parser responses retain exact stdout, stderr and status bytes. The updated real CLI suite passes 11/0, including help/version success and refusal failure; all-target deny-warnings Clippy passes. Full gates and release timing will be refreshed for this production change. The completed prior local aggregate remains evidence for 6687ef9, not the new parser code."
  "2026-10-18T08:13:26.831Z",codex-agent,"Production 309df2e linked acceptance passed again: pm test pm-rust-xb3s --run --progress executed all 12 orientation differentials, exit 0, elapsed 99711 ms. Automatic result recording remains disabled by project policy; this is its persistent comment receipt. The refreshed release receipt has 30 runs per command/runtime and all 240 raw samples: native/oracle p50 ms context 2592.8/3355.3, list 2116.0/1269.9, search history 2200.0/4177.7, get 1864.8/1118.5. Nice 15, 4 CPUs, one-minute load range 13.84-25.64; document includes p95 and complete load averages. All 6004 original authoritative files and copied equivalents still hash unchanged. Measured binary SHA-256 01732ddadf6f6d0f25efe74b5b8eabb12d8b571437d0095b9f4fc6212ed05447. New release still matches full public-copy context bytes (11839 JSON, 7219 TOON) and all six parser before/after responses. Fresh npm registry version is 2026.10.18; the required oracle remains locked at 2026.10.14. Linux aggregate CI is green; remaining validation continues."
  "2026-10-18T08:29:39.042Z",codex-agent,"Acceptance at 309df2e: isolated RUST_TEST_THREADS=8 just release-check passes 449 normal and 449 instrumented tests across 20 suites each, zero failures/ignored. Linux coverage is 11656/11656 lines, 19104/19104 regions, 1170/1170 functions and 2830/2830 branches (100% each). Fmt, pedantic deny-warnings Clippy, private rustdoc, identity audit, cargo audit and changelog check pass. Strict read-only health passes eight checks with four advisory findings retained. All six OS test/aggregate CI jobs and both security checks are green. CI normal counts: Linux 449, macOS 445, Windows 441. Windows now reaches 11655/11655 lines, 19105/19105 regions, 1171/1171 functions and 2832/2832 branches, closing the immediate-exit regression seen at 6687ef9 (2 lines, 3 regions, 2 branches missed). No thresholds, exclusions or coverage-only production conditions changed. Six behavioral revert controls and six parser byte-preservation cases are documented. The new linked PM test passes 12/0; tracking_disabled is recorded explicitly. Final measured latency and all 240 samples are linked in docs, alongside zero changed hashes across 6004 original/copy authoritative files. Releasing the claim for orchestrator review of draft PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/92; all items remain open."
  "2026-10-18T09:41:44.537Z",codex-agent,"Review round: rechecked the clean PR branch and existing items; origin/main is already included. Addressing all three unresolved review threads and reviewer issue #93 in this PR with independent behavioral revert proofs. Read-performance work remains deferred to its existing follow-up. Rust acceptance uses the documented just release-check plus strict tracker health, including a fresh no-local clone; npm/Bun release scripts do not exist in this Rust crate."
  "2026-10-18T09:48:46.418Z",codex-agent,"Review findings reproduced with new tests against the prior code: unrelated search/create/get values were misclassified; non-Unicode environment data panicked; non-active configured progress underflowed; and dangling parent traversal omitted the missing edge. Fixes retain Clap diagnostics, collect lossy OS strings, count progress within active items with custom focus-classification receipts, and append deduplicated dangling scalar references in oracle order. Independent single-fix reversions and complete Rust gates are next. Issue #93 is included; the read-performance follow-up remains untouched."
  "2026-10-18T09:49:36.573Z",codex-agent,"Independent single-fix behavioral reverts confirmed: cargo test --locked --test cli_dispatch orientation_values_do_not_reclassify_unrelated_commands failed 0/1 with only command detection reverted; cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential context_non_unicode_environment_matches_oracle failed 0/1 with only OS-string collection reverted; cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential context_non_active_progress_matches_oracle failed 0/1 with only the active-progress filter reverted; cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_dangling_parents_match_oracle failed 0/1 with only dependency index construction reverted. Each exited 101 on a behavioral assertion, not compilation. All other fixes and all new tests remained present. The parent regression covers ten controls across tree/graph/summary, JSON/TOON and normal/depth-zero bounds, including unchanged item/history bytes."
  "2026-10-18T09:49:47.852Z",codex-agent,"The additional classification regression also failed independently: cargo test --locked --lib custom_focus_classification_survives_compaction exited 101 with only finalize_orientation restored to the previous implementation. All five negative controls completed; fixed source bytes were restored exactly. The custom lifecycle correction follows the real oracle: progress is counted within active items, rather than saturating a subtraction of differently defined sets. Its retained focus-state receipt preserves custom progress identity through output compaction."
  "2026-10-18T09:55:05.077Z",codex-agent,"Positive review controls: unrelated-command dispatch passed 1/0; non-Unicode context and custom lifecycle context pass exact oracle bytes, including explicit token budgets; custom classification compaction passed 1/0; dangling parents passed all 120 projection/encoding/bound comparisons. The first PM-linked suite was interrupted by an overlapping oracle reinstall (14 passed, one module-not-found failure); this was an execution-order mistake, not parity evidence. Oracle installs and the final PM-linked test will run serially. The full isolated Rust release gate is running with unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T10:27:06.571Z",codex-agent,"The isolated just release-check normal pass completed: 454 passed, zero failed, zero ignored across 20 suites. All 15 orientation differentials passed, including 120 dangling-parent comparisons, and the 12-test CLI dispatch suite passed. Fmt, pedantic deny-warnings Clippy and private rustdoc passed. The unchanged-threshold instrumented pass is now running; coverage is not yet claimed for this revision."
  "2026-10-18T10:51:10.372Z",codex-agent,"The first full review gate passed all 454 normal and all 454 instrumented tests but failed unchanged coverage thresholds: two lines/regions and two branches were uncovered. Direct SDK custom-progress acceptance covers the library receipt path. The other gap exposed a prior deps mismatch: the pinned oracle renders the no-active-blocker scalar as a missing blocked_by edge. cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_no_active_blocker_matches_oracle failed 0/1 with exit 101 and only that suppression present; removing the suppression matches the oracle. Twelve additional real-CLI projection/encoding/bound controls and read-only bytes cover this behavior. A fresh complete gate and serial PM-linked rerun will follow; no coverage claim is made from the failed gate."
  "2026-10-18T10:53:08.713Z",codex-agent,"Coverage follow-up positive controls pass: cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential deps_no_active_blocker_matches_oracle passed 1/0 (12 real comparisons), cargo test --locked --lib custom_progress_receipts_use_active_summary_counts passed 1/0, and cargo test --locked --lib dependency_alias_and_scalar_boundaries passed 1/0. Pedantic Clippy passed. The sentinel regression failed 0/1 with exit 101 before removing only the suppression and passed after removal; the remaining review fixes stayed present. This matches the pinned oracle rather than changing its sentinel semantics. A second complete isolated release gate will certify the resulting source at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T10:54:36.159Z",codex-agent,"The direct SDK context regression independently failed with exit 101 after reverting only the active-progress filter, then passed after exact source restoration. The final tracker test plan now links orientation differentials, real-process CLI dispatch and direct library acceptance. Seven negative test runs cover the four review findings, custom compaction, the pinned sentinel behavior and the direct SDK entrypoint. The second complete gate is running; its expected Linux normal count is 456 and orientation count is 16."
  "2026-10-18T11:22:04.523Z",codex-agent,"Second aggregate: all 456 normal and 456 instrumented tests passed; branches 2834/2834 and functions 1177/1177 reached 100%, but the unchanged gate retained one uncovered context line/region (11731/11732 lines, 19211/19212 regions). The remaining path is a focus-state match arm across the SDK/CLI builds. Acceptance now includes active custom progress through the direct SDK and a separate ordinary blocked row through the real CLI. Production source is unchanged by this final coverage correction. An incremental diagnostic precedes another clean complete gate; neither failed aggregate is reported as passing."
  "2026-10-18T11:57:46.827Z",codex-agent,"Final clean review acceptance: isolated just release-check passed 456 normal and 456 instrumented tests across 20 suites each, zero failed/ignored. Complete source coverage is lines 11732/11732, regions 19212/19212, functions 1177/1177 and branches 2834/2834, all 100% at unchanged thresholds. Fmt, pedantic Clippy, private rustdoc, identity, audit and changelog passed; audit retains one pre-existing allowed unsafe-libyaml unmaintained warning. The final serial pm test --run --progress --fail-on-skipped --fail-on-empty-test-run passed all three linked commands: orientation 16, CLI dispatch 12, library 235 (263 total). Automatic result recording remains disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt. All three review threads and issue #93 are addressed; read-performance work is untouched. Seven negative controls are recorded above. Claim will be released for orchestrator verification; no item is closed. Fresh-clone health and final-head CI will be verified and recorded in PR #92 after committing."
  "2026-10-18T12:22:10.383Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI on ad0169b passed all three normal OS jobs (Linux456, macOS452, Windows447), both security checks, and the Windows aggregate with 100% all four dimensions. Linux and macOS aggregate jobs were cancelled by their 20-minute timeout while instrumented tests were still progressing; Windows had a 30-minute budget. These cancellations are missing evidence, not approval. Reclaimed the item to correct only CI runtime capacity while preserving the complete test/coverage gates, then rerun final-head CI. Production Rust source and the completed latency receipt remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T12:25:14.449Z",codex-agent,"CI capacity correction verified against GitHub job annotations: Linux job 117669461040 and macOS job 117669460775 in run 39125433531 both report exceeded maximum execution time of 20m0s; Windows aggregate completed with 100% lines11731/11731, regions19213/19213, functions1178/1178, branches2836/2836. Aggregate timeout is now 35 minutes for every OS, within the review wait window. Rust source, Rust tests, dependency pins, justfile gate commands, coverage thresholds and disabled release automation are byte-unchanged from certified ad0169b. The existing workflow-contract command passed 18/0 through pm test --run --only-last --progress with strict skipped/empty checks; the earlier three linked commands passed 263/0. Actual old-limit cancellations are the negative runtime evidence; final-head CI must supply positive evidence. No mirrored timeout assertion or skipped gate was introduced. Releasing the claim for the final rerun; no item is closed."
  "2026-10-18T13:04:01.348Z",codex-agent,"Review round on c511d60: read all three unresolved threads, newest full review and open issue #93. Branch is current with origin/main and clean before changes. Fix rejected Clap token reporting, build the dependency corpus identity set once, and validate normalized history filenames before lookup. Add focused regressions and single-fix negative controls, retain issue #93 differential evidence, then run the documented Rust release gate and strict PM health. No broader read-performance work; deferred items remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-18T13:08:09.623Z",codex-agent,"Second full-review fixes implemented. Parser refusals now use Clap InvalidArg context (including extra positional tokens and short flags); fallback excludes allowed flags. History validates normalized filenames before corpus decoding and path existence, and invalid IDs retain the oracle invalid_argument_value envelope. Twelve real CLI invalid-filename comparisons match exact stderr/status with an escaped file present and absent; SDK acceptance includes NUL, dot identities and a corrupt corpus. Dependency indexing collects corpus keys once and reuses normalized scalar targets; the deterministic 256-item normalization budget is test-only instrumentation and does not start the separate selective-read work."
  "2026-10-18T13:08:10.562Z",codex-agent,"Three single-fix behavioral revert proofs rebuilt and failed with exit 101, then passed with exit 0 after exact source restoration: cargo test --locked --test cli_dispatch orientation_refusals_name_the_rejected_argument (only rejected-token selection restored); cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential history_invalid_filename_matches_oracle (only pre-lookup filename check removed, native exits 3 versus oracle 2); cargo test --locked --lib dependency_identity_normalization_has_a_linear_budget (only index function restored to repeated corpus scan, exceeding 4096 normalizations for 256 items). All source bytes restored exactly; focused parser-context, history CLI/SDK and dependency tests pass. Existing issue #93 differential controls retained."
  "2026-10-18T13:11:34.170Z",codex-agent,"Health scope receipt: documented Rust CI health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit passes with 8 checks and 4 inherited advisories locally. Full health --strict-exit additionally reports the two inherited history discontinuities already tracked by pm-rust-b4yl; fresh prior-head clone reproduces them and their authoritative bytes are unchanged. Host-loaded extension version skew disappears under isolated HOME; configuration is unchanged. Full historical integrity is not claimed. npm and Bun release scripts do not apply because this Rust repository has no root package.json; just release-check is the documented aggregate and is running with isolated identity."
  "2026-10-18T13:21:36.718Z",codex-agent,"Second-round linked acceptance: pm test pm-rust-xb3s --run --progress --json passes all five exact linked commands under isolated identity: cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential 17/0; cargo test --locked --test cli_dispatch 14/0; cargo test --locked --lib 237/0; cargo test --locked --test release_pipeline_contract 18/0; cargo test --locked --bin pm-rust 24/0. Total 310 passed, zero failed or ignored. Result recording remains disabled by existing project policy (tracking_disabled), so this comment is the persistent receipt; configuration unchanged. Native and oracle strictly verified the feature stream before this receipt, matching all 65 records in 15656 JSON bytes with empty stderr."
  "2026-10-18T13:38:15.664Z",codex-agent,"Clean second-review release gate passed under isolated identity: RUST_TEST_THREADS=8 just release-check. All 462 normal and 462 branch-instrumented tests passed across 20 suites each, with zero failures or ignored tests. Coverage: 11743/11743 lines, 19246/19246 regions, 1179/1179 functions, 2834/2834 branches, all 100 percent at unchanged thresholds and source scope. Fmt, pedantic deny-warnings Clippy, private rustdoc, identity, cargo audit and changelog checks passed. Audit retains the one previously allowed unsafe-libyaml unmaintained warning. Source/test digests remained unchanged. The 310-test linked runner and all three single-fix revert controls passed. Documented CI health passed; inherited full-health chain drift remains separately recorded in pm-rust-b4yl. Implementation is ready for push and final-head CI; final platform receipts will be in PR #92. Release stays disabled; broader read-performance work remains unstarted."
